summary:
@jaschasd This has been an amazing collaboration to be a part of and the submitted tasks were tremendously creative!
LLMs haven't yet mastered checkmate ... but they are learning legal chess moves and how to identify movies from emojis!
📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FU2tWzyUEAATmXP.jpg

Thank you! The Brier score measure, and the impetus to look at model calibration, were both extremely important contributions!
Quoting @realSharonZhou
@jaschasd Excited to have been part of 1/442nd of this huge effort for benchmarking LLMs! Thanks, organizers, for leading the charge.

This is a fascinating task, on which the performance of the largest models is still close to chance and not obviously increasing with scale.
Quoting @allenainie
@tobigerstenberg and I collected 190 stories from 30 Philosophy/CogSci papers published between 1989 and 2021 to test LLM on the task of selecting a true cause in a text scenario. LLMs don't choose causes similar to human. Check out our dataset here:
